1
00:00:01,020 --> 00:00:04,080
part 3 chapter 6.

2
00:00:04,080 --> 00:00:06,477
The Chestnut Tree was almost empty.

3
00:00:06,477 --> 00:00:10,919
A ray of sunlight slanting through a window fell on dusty tabletops

4
00:00:10,919 --> 00:00:13,558
It was the lonely hour of 15.

5
00:00:13,558 --> 00:00:17,520
A teeny music trickled from the telescreens.

6
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:21,477
Winston said in his usual corner, gazing into an empty glass.

7
00:00:21,477 --> 00:00:26,340
Now and again he glanced up at a vast face which eyed him from the opposite wall.

8
00:00:26,340 --> 00:00:30,240
BIG BROTHER IS WATCHING YOU, the captain said.

9
00:00:30,240 --> 00:00:34,740
Unbidden, a waiter came and filled his glass up with Victory Gin, shaking into

10
00:00:34,740 --> 00:00:38,159
it a few drops from another bottle with a quilt through the cork.

11
00:00:38,159 --> 00:00:42,419
It was saccharin flavored with cloves, the specialty of the cafe

12
00:00:42,419 --> 00:00:47,159
Winston was listening to the telescreen the present-only music was coming out of

13
00:00:47,159 --> 00:00:50,457
it, but there was a possibility that at any moment there might be a special

14
00:00:50,457 --> 00:00:53,340
bulletin from the Ministry of Peace.

15
00:00:53,340 --> 00:00:57,419
The news from the African front was disquieting in the extreme.

16
00:00:57,419 --> 00:01:00,840
On and off he had been worrying about it all day.

17
00:01:00,840 --> 00:01:06,119
A Eurasian army (Oceania was at war with Eurasia: Oceania had always been at war

18
00:01:06,119 --> 00:01:10,500
with Eurasia) was moving southward at a terrifying speed.

19
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:14,340
The midday bulletin had not mentioned any definite area, but it was probable

20
00:01:14,340 --> 00:01:20,520
that already the mouth of the Congo was a battlefield razaville and Leopoldville were in danger.

21
00:01:20,520 --> 00:01:23,637
One did not have to look at the map to see what it meant.

22
00:01:23,637 --> 00:01:27,957
It was not merely a question of losing Central Africa: for the first time in the

23
00:01:27,957 --> 00:01:31,558
whole war, the territory of Oceania itself was menaced.

24
00:01:31,558 --> 00:01:35,759
A violent emotion, not fear exactly but a sort of undifferentiated excitement,

25
00:01:35,759 --> 00:01:38,759
flared up in him, then faded again.

26
00:01:38,759 --> 00:01:41,040
He stopped thinking about the war.

27
00:01:41,040 --> 00:01:44,520
In these days he could never fix his mind on any one subject for more than a

28
00:01:44,520 --> 00:01:46,259
few moments at a time.

29
00:01:46,259 --> 00:01:49,319
He picked up his glass and drained it at a gulp.

30
00:01:49,319 --> 00:01:53,099
As always the gin made him shudder and even Rich slightly.

31
00:01:53,099 --> 00:01:55,020
The stuff was horrible.

32
00:01:55,020 --> 00:01:58,378
The cloves and saccharin themselves disgusting enough in their sickly way,

33
00:01:58,378 --> 00:02:02,759
could not disguise the flat oily smell; and what was worst of all was that the

34
00:02:02,759 --> 00:02:07,137
smell of gin, which dwelt with him night and day, was inextricably mixed up in his

35
00:02:07,137 --> 00:02:11,457
mind with the smell of those——— He never named them, even in his thoughts,

36
00:02:11,457 --> 00:02:15,540
and so far as it was possible he never visualized them there was something that

37
00:02:15,540 --> 00:02:21,477
he was half aware of, hovering close to his face, a smell that clung to his nostrils.

38
00:02:21,477 --> 00:02:25,259
As the gin rose in him he belched through purple lips.

39
00:02:25,259 --> 00:02:28,860
He had grown fatter since they released him, and had regained his old color

40
00:02:28,860 --> 00:02:33,419
indeed, more than regained it. His features had thickened, the skin on nose

41
00:02:33,419 --> 00:02:37,977
and cheekbones was coarsely read even the bald scalp was too deep a pink.

42
00:02:37,977 --> 00:02:42,297
A waiter, again unbidden, brought the chessboard into the current issue of the

43
00:02:42,297 --> 00:02:46,080
Times, with the page turned down at the chess problem.

44
00:02:46,080 --> 00:02:50,457
Then, seeing that Winston's glass was empty, he brought the gin bottle and filled it.

45
00:02:50,457 --> 00:02:54,297
There was no need to give orders. They knew his habits. The chessboard was

46
00:02:54,297 --> 00:02:58,680
always waiting for him, his corner table was always reserved; even when the place

47
00:02:58,680 --> 00:03:04,319
was full he had it to himself, since nobody cared to be seen sitting too close to him.

48
00:03:04,319 --> 00:03:07,200
He never even bothered to count his drinks.

49
00:03:07,200 --> 00:03:10,619
At irregular intervals they presented him with a dirty slip of paper which

50
00:03:10,619 --> 00:03:14,040
they said was the bill, but he had the impression that they always undercharged

51
00:03:14,040 --> 00:03:18,119
him. It would have made no difference if it had been the other way about.

52
00:03:18,119 --> 00:03:20,218
He had always plenty of money nowadays.

53
00:03:20,218 --> 00:03:26,340
He even had a job, a cynical more highly paid than his old job had been.

54
00:03:26,340 --> 00:03:31,378
The music from the telescreen stopped and a voice took over. Winston raised his head to listen.

55
00:03:31,378 --> 00:03:33,840
No bulletins from the front, however.

56
00:03:33,840 --> 00:03:37,378
It was merely a brief announcement from the Ministry of Plenty.

57
00:03:37,378 --> 00:03:40,919
In the preceding quarter, it appeared, the 10th Three-Year Plan's quota for

58
00:03:40,919 --> 00:03:47,218
bootlesses had been over fulfilled by 98 percent He examined the chess problem and set

59
00:03:47,218 --> 00:03:52,137
out the pieces. It was a tricky ending, involving a couple of nights likes to

60
00:03:52,137 --> 00:03:57,000
play and mate in two moves.' Winston looked up at the portrait of Big Brother.

61
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:00,718
White always mates, he thought with a sort of cloudy mysticism.

62
00:04:00,718 --> 00:04:03,779
Always, without exception, it is so arranged.

63
00:04:03,779 --> 00:04:07,619
In no chess problem since the beginning of the world has black ever won.

64
00:04:07,619 --> 00:04:12,058
Did it not symbolize the eternal, unvarying triumph of Good over Evil?

65
00:04:12,058 --> 00:04:15,898
The huge face gazed back at him, full of calm power.

66
00:04:15,898 --> 00:04:18,840
White always mates.

67
00:04:18,840 --> 00:04:23,700
The voice from the telescreen paused and added in a different and much greater tone:

68
00:04:23,700 --> 00:04:28,977
'You will want to stand by for an important announcement at 15 30. 1530

69
00:04:28,977 --> 00:04:31,319
This is news of the highest importance.

70
00:04:31,319 --> 00:04:37,558
Take care not to miss it 1530 The tinkling music struck up again.

71
00:04:37,558 --> 00:04:42,119
Winston's heart stirred. That was the bulletin from the front; instinct told

72
00:04:42,119 --> 00:04:44,520
him that it was bad news that was coming.

73
00:04:44,520 --> 00:04:48,297
All day, with little spurts of excitement to the thought of a smashing defeat in

74
00:04:48,297 --> 00:04:50,759
Africa had been in and out of his mind.

75
00:04:50,759 --> 00:04:54,240
He seemed actually to see the Eurasian army swarming across the never broken

76
00:04:54,240 --> 00:04:58,797
frontier and pouring down into the tip of Africa like a column of ants

77
00:04:58,797 --> 00:05:03,419
or I had not been possible to outflank them in some way? The outline of the West

78
00:05:03,419 --> 00:05:06,659
African coast stood out vividly in his mind.

79
00:05:06,659 --> 00:05:10,020
He picked up the white knight and moved it across the board.

80
00:05:10,020 --> 00:05:11,939
There was the proper spot.

81
00:05:11,939 --> 00:05:15,419
Even while he saw the black horde racing southward he saw another force,

82
00:05:15,419 --> 00:05:19,680
mysteriously assembled, suddenly planted in their rear, cutting their

83
00:05:19,680 --> 00:05:23,637
communications by land and sea. He filtered that by willing it he was

84
00:05:23,637 --> 00:05:25,319
bringing that other force into existence.

85
00:05:25,319 --> 00:05:28,137
But it was necessary to act quickly.

86
00:05:28,137 --> 00:05:31,680
If they could get control of the whole of Africa, if they had airfields and

87
00:05:31,680 --> 00:05:35,580
submarine bases of the Cape, it would cut Oceania in two.

88
00:05:35,580 --> 00:05:39,840
It might mean anything: defeat, breakdown, the re-division of the world, the

89
00:05:39,840 --> 00:05:41,520
destruction of the Party!

90
00:05:41,520 --> 00:05:46,200
He drew a deep breath. An extraordinary medley of feeling but it was not a

91
00:05:46,200 --> 00:05:50,099
meddling exactly; rather it was successive layers of feeling, in which

92
00:05:50,099 --> 00:05:54,898
one could not say which layer was undermost— —struggled inside him

93
00:05:54,898 --> 00:05:59,340
spasm passed. He put the white knight back in its place, but for the moment he

94
00:05:59,340 --> 00:06:02,218
could not settle down to serious study of the chess problem.

95
00:06:02,218 --> 00:06:06,297
His thoughts wandered again. Almost unconsciously he traced with his finger

96
00:06:06,297 --> 00:06:11,340
in the dust of the table two plus two equals five

97
00:06:11,340 --> 00:06:13,919
They can't get inside you,' she had said.

98
00:06:13,919 --> 00:06:16,137
But they could get inside you.

99
00:06:16,137 --> 00:06:19,680
'What happens to you here is forever O'Brien had said.

100
00:06:19,680 --> 00:06:24,659
That was a true word. There were things, your own acts, from which you could never recover.

101
00:06:24,659 --> 00:06:30,137
Something was killed in your breast: burnt out cauterized out.

102
00:06:30,297 --> 00:06:33,718
He had seen her; he had even spoken to her.

103
00:06:33,718 --> 00:06:37,439
There was no danger in it. He knew as though instinctively that they now took

104
00:06:37,439 --> 00:06:39,599
almost no interest in his doings.

105
00:06:39,599 --> 00:06:43,740
He could have arranged to meet her a second time if either of them had wanted to.

106
00:06:43,740 --> 00:06:46,319
Actually it was by chance that they had met.

107
00:06:46,319 --> 00:06:50,700
It was in the Park, on a vile, biting day in March, when the earth was like iron

108
00:06:50,700 --> 00:06:54,119
and all the grass seemed dead and there was not a bud anywhere except a few

109
00:06:54,119 --> 00:06:58,378
crocuses Richard pushed themselves up to be dismembered by the wind.

110
00:06:58,378 --> 00:07:02,819
He was hurrying along with frozen hands and watering eyes when he saw her not 10

111
00:07:02,819 --> 00:07:04,500
meters away from him.

112
00:07:04,500 --> 00:07:08,279
It struck him at once that she had changed in some ill-defined way.

113
00:07:08,279 --> 00:07:13,020
They almost passed one another without a sign, then he turned and followed her, not

114
00:07:13,020 --> 00:07:18,360
very eagerly. He knew that there was no danger, nobody would take any interest in him

115
00:07:18,360 --> 00:07:19,977
She did not speak.

116
00:07:19,977 --> 00:07:23,340
She walked obliquely away across the grass as though trying to get rid of him,

117
00:07:23,340 --> 00:07:27,297
then seemed to resign herself to having him at her side.

118
00:07:27,297 --> 00:07:31,259
Presently they were in among a clump of ragged leafless shrubs, useless either

119
00:07:31,259 --> 00:07:34,020
for concealment or as protection from the wind.

120
00:07:34,020 --> 00:07:39,000
They halted. It was vitally cold. The wind whistled through the twigs and fretted

121
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:41,398
the occasional dirty looking crocuses.

122
00:07:41,398 --> 00:07:44,040
He put his arm around her waist.

123
00:07:44,040 --> 00:07:49,020
There was no telescreen, but they must be hidden microphones: besides, they could be seen.

124
00:07:49,020 --> 00:07:51,540
It did not matter, nothing mattered.

125
00:07:51,540 --> 00:07:55,378
They could have laid down on the ground and done that if they had wanted to.

126
00:07:55,378 --> 00:07:58,680
His flesh froze with horror as the thought of it.

127
00:07:58,680 --> 00:08:03,297
She made no response whatever to the clasp of his arm; she did not even try to

128
00:08:03,297 --> 00:08:04,919
disengage herself.

129
00:08:04,919 --> 00:08:09,957
He knew now what had changed in her face was sallower, and there was a long scar,

130
00:08:09,957 --> 00:08:15,540
partly hidden by the hair, across a foreign temple; but that was not the change.

131
00:08:15,540 --> 00:08:20,457
It was that her waist had grown thicker, and, in a surprising way, had stiffened. He

132
00:08:20,457 --> 00:08:25,259
remembered her once, after the explosion of a rocket bomb, he had helped to drag a

133
00:08:25,259 --> 00:08:28,680
corpse out of some ruins, and had been astonished not only by the incredible

134
00:08:28,680 --> 00:08:32,759
weight of the thing, but by its rigidity and awkwardness to handle, which made it

135
00:08:32,759 --> 00:08:34,977
seem more like stone than flesh.

136
00:08:34,977 --> 00:08:39,119
Her body felt like that. It occurred to him that the texture of her skin would

137
00:08:39,119 --> 00:08:42,599
be quite different from what it once had been.

138
00:08:42,599 --> 00:08:45,540
He did not attempt to kiss her, nor did they speak.

139
00:08:45,540 --> 00:08:50,398
As they walked back across the grass she looked directly at him for the first time.

140
00:08:50,398 --> 00:08:54,180
It was only a momentary glance, full of contempt and dislike.

141
00:08:54,180 --> 00:08:57,840
He wondered whether it was a dislike that came purely out of the past or

142
00:08:57,840 --> 00:09:01,740
whether it was inspired also by his bloated face and the water that the wind

143
00:09:01,740 --> 00:09:04,080
kept squeezing from his eyes.

144
00:09:04,080 --> 00:09:08,700
They sat down on two iron chairs, side by side but not too close together.

145
00:09:08,700 --> 00:09:12,957
He saw that she was about to speak. She moved to a clumsy shoe a few centimeters

146
00:09:12,957 --> 00:09:15,419
into deliberately crushed a twig.

147
00:09:15,419 --> 00:09:19,439
Her feet seemed to have grown broader, he noticed.

148
00:09:19,439 --> 00:09:24,659
'I betrayed you,' she said boldly I betrayed you,' he said.

149
00:09:24,659 --> 00:09:29,040
She gave him another quick look of dislike. 'Sometimes,' she said, 'they threaten

150
00:09:29,040 --> 00:09:32,759
you with something— —something you can't stand up to, can't even think about.

151
00:09:32,759 --> 00:09:34,919
And then you say, "Don't do it to me, do it

152
00:09:34,919 --> 00:09:40,137
to somebody else, do it to so and so And perhaps you might pretend, afterwards,

153
00:09:40,137 --> 00:09:43,500
that it was only a trick and that you just said it to make them stop and

154
00:09:43,500 --> 00:09:45,058
didn't really mean it.

155
00:09:45,058 --> 00:09:50,099
But that isn't true. At the time when it happens you do mean it. You think there's

156
00:09:50,099 --> 00:09:54,718
no other way of saving yourself, and you're quite ready to save yourself that way.

157
00:09:54,718 --> 00:09:56,759
You wanted to happen to the other person.

158
00:09:56,759 --> 00:09:58,977
You don't give a damn what they suffer.

159
00:09:58,977 --> 00:10:01,740
All you care about is yourself.'

160
00:10:01,740 --> 00:10:06,779
'All you care about is yourself here code And after that, you don't feel the same

161
00:10:06,779 --> 00:10:09,180
towards the other person any longer.'

162
00:10:09,180 --> 00:10:13,159
'No,' he said, 'you don't feel the same.'

163
00:10:13,378 --> 00:10:17,279
There did not seem to be anything more to say. The wind blastered their thin

164
00:10:17,279 --> 00:10:19,137
overalls against their bodies.

165
00:10:19,137 --> 00:10:23,520
Almost at once it became embarrassing to sit there in silence: besides, it was too

166
00:10:23,520 --> 00:10:25,080
cold to keep still.

167
00:10:25,080 --> 00:10:28,860
She said something about catching her Tube and stood up to go.

168
00:10:28,860 --> 00:10:31,200
'We must meet again,' he said.

169
00:10:31,200 --> 00:10:35,218
'Yes,' she said, 'we must meet again.'

170
00:10:35,218 --> 00:10:39,957
He followed irresolutely for a little distance, half a pace behind her.

171
00:10:39,957 --> 00:10:42,058
They did not speak again.

172
00:10:42,058 --> 00:10:46,020
She did not actually try to shake him off, but walked at just such a speed as

173
00:10:46,020 --> 00:10:48,180
to prevent his keeping abreast of her.

174
00:10:48,180 --> 00:10:51,718
He had made up his mind that he would accompany her as far as the Tube station,

175
00:10:51,718 --> 00:10:56,817
but suddenly this process of trailing along in the cold seemed pointless and unbearable.

176
00:10:56,817 --> 00:11:01,137
He was overwhelmed by a desire not so much to get away from Julia as to get

177
00:11:01,137 --> 00:11:04,919
back to the Chestnut Tree Cafe which had never seemed so attractive as at this

178
00:11:04,919 --> 00:11:09,240
moment. He had a nostalgic vision of his corner table, with the newspaper in the

179
00:11:09,240 --> 00:11:11,759
chessboard and the ever flowing gin.

180
00:11:11,759 --> 00:11:14,218
Above all it would be warm in there.

181
00:11:14,218 --> 00:11:17,878
The next moment, not all together by accident, he allowed himself to become

182
00:11:17,878 --> 00:11:20,817
separated from her by a small knot of people.

183
00:11:20,817 --> 00:11:25,137
He made a half-hearted attempt to catch up, then slowed down, turned and made off

184
00:11:25,137 --> 00:11:27,119
in the opposite direction.

185
00:11:27,119 --> 00:11:31,317
When he had gone 50 meters he looked back. The street was not crowded, but

186
00:11:31,317 --> 00:11:33,297
already he could not distinguish her.

187
00:11:33,297 --> 00:11:36,419
Any one of a dozen hurrying figures might have been hers.

188
00:11:36,419 --> 00:11:41,398
Perhaps her thickened, stiffened body was no longer recognizable from behind.

189
00:11:41,398 --> 00:11:43,619
'At the time when it happens,' she had said,

190
00:11:43,619 --> 00:11:49,378
'you do mean it.' He had meant it. He had not merely said it, he had wished it.

191
00:11:49,378 --> 00:11:53,878
He had wished that she and not he should be delivered over to the———

192
00:11:53,878 --> 00:11:58,020
Something changed in the music that trickled from the telescreen cracked and

193
00:11:58,020 --> 00:12:00,898
jeering note, a yellow note, came into it.

194
00:12:00,898 --> 00:12:04,919
And then— —perhaps it was not happening, perhaps it was only a memory taking on

195
00:12:04,919 --> 00:12:10,919
the semblance of sound— —a voice was singing: Under the spreading chestnut tree I sold

196
00:12:10,919 --> 00:12:15,477
you and you sold me— The tears welled up in his eyes.

197
00:12:15,477 --> 00:12:20,580
A passing waiter noticed that his glass was empty and came back with the gin bottle.

198
00:12:20,580 --> 00:12:23,398
He took up his glass and sniffed at it.

199
00:12:23,398 --> 00:12:27,659
The stuff grew not less but more horrible with every mouthful he drank.

200
00:12:27,659 --> 00:12:30,000
But it had become the element he swam in.

201
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:33,419
It was his life, his death and his resurrection.

202
00:12:33,419 --> 00:12:38,637
It was gin that sank him into stupor every night, and the gin that revived him every morning.

203
00:12:38,637 --> 00:12:43,378
When he woke, seldom before 1100 with gummed up eyelids and fiery mouth and a

204
00:12:43,378 --> 00:12:46,797
back that seemed to be broken, it would have been impossible even to

205
00:12:46,797 --> 00:12:50,759
rise from the horizontal if it had not been for the bottle and teacup placed

206
00:12:50,759 --> 00:12:52,919
beside the bed overnight.

207
00:12:52,919 --> 00:12:56,580
Through the midday hours he sat with glazed face, the bottle handy, listening

208
00:12:56,580 --> 00:13:01,619
to the telescreen. From 15 to closing time he was a fixture in the Chestnut Tree.

209
00:13:01,619 --> 00:13:07,137
No one cared what he did any longer, no whistle woke him, no telescreen admonished him.

210
00:13:07,137 --> 00:13:10,680
Occasionally, perhaps twice a week, he went to a dusty forgotten looking office

211
00:13:10,680 --> 00:13:14,637
in the Ministry of Truth and did a little work, or what was called work.

212
00:13:14,637 --> 00:13:18,659
He had been appointed to a subcommittee of a subcommittee which had sprouted

213
00:13:18,659 --> 00:13:22,080
from one of the innumerable committees dealing with minor difficulties that

214
00:13:22,080 --> 00:13:26,340
arose in the compilation of the 11th Edition of the Newspeak Dictionary.

215
00:13:26,340 --> 00:13:29,759
They were engaged in producing something called an Interim Report,

216
00:13:29,759 --> 00:13:33,898
but what it was that they were reporting on he had never definitely found out.

217
00:13:33,898 --> 00:13:36,957
It was something to do with the question of whether Commerce should be placed

218
00:13:36,957 --> 00:13:39,297
inside brackets, or outside.

219
00:13:39,297 --> 00:13:43,558
There were four others on the committee, all of them persons similar to himself.

220
00:13:43,558 --> 00:13:47,457
There were days when they assembled and then promptly dispersed again, frankly

221
00:13:47,457 --> 00:13:50,700
admitting to one another that there was not really anything to be done.

222
00:13:50,700 --> 00:13:53,580
But there were other days when they settled down to their work almost

223
00:13:53,580 --> 00:13:57,779
eagerly, making a tremendous show of entering up their minutes and drafting

224
00:13:57,779 --> 00:14:02,040
long memoranda which were never finished— when the argument as to what they were

225
00:14:02,040 --> 00:14:05,637
supposedly arguing about grew extraordinarily involved and abstruse,

226
00:14:05,637 --> 00:14:10,860
with subtle haggling over definitions, enormous digressions, quarrels— —threats,

227
00:14:10,860 --> 00:14:13,439
even, to appeal to higher authority.

228
00:14:13,439 --> 00:14:16,439
And then suddenly the life would go out of them and they would sit around the

229
00:14:16,439 --> 00:14:22,398
table looking at one another with extinct eyes, like ghosts fading at Crow

230
00:14:22,398 --> 00:14:25,317
The telescreen was silent for a moment.

231
00:14:25,317 --> 00:14:27,477
Winston raised his head again.

232
00:14:27,477 --> 00:14:31,680
The bulletin! But no, they were merely changing the music.

233
00:14:31,680 --> 00:14:36,957
He had the map of Africa behind his eyelids. The movement of the armies was a diagram:

234
00:14:36,957 --> 00:14:40,977
a black arrow tearing vertically southward, and a white arrow horizontally

235
00:14:40,977 --> 00:14:43,500
eastward, across the tail of the first.

236
00:14:43,500 --> 00:14:47,817
As though for reassurance he looked up at the imperturbable face in the portrait.

237
00:14:47,817 --> 00:14:51,680
Was it conceivable that the second arrow did not even exist?

238
00:14:51,680 --> 00:14:56,279
His interest flagged again. He drank another mouthful of gin, picked up the

239
00:14:56,279 --> 00:14:58,378
white knight and made a tentative move.

240
00:14:58,378 --> 00:14:59,580
Check.

241
00:14:59,580 --> 00:15:06,119
But it was evidently not the right move, because——— Uncalled, a memory floated into his mind.

242
00:15:06,119 --> 00:15:10,797
He saw a candle-lit room with a vast white counterpaint bed, and himself, a boy

243
00:15:10,797 --> 00:15:15,360
of nine or ten, sitting on the floor, shaking a dice box and laughing excitedly.

244
00:15:15,360 --> 00:15:18,840
His mother was sitting opposite him and also laughing.

245
00:15:18,840 --> 00:15:22,680
It must have been about a month before she disappeared. It was a moment of

246
00:15:22,680 --> 00:15:26,340
reconciliation, when the nagging hunger in his belly was forgotten and his

247
00:15:26,340 --> 00:15:29,637
earlier affection for her had temporarily revived.

248
00:15:29,637 --> 00:15:33,540
He remembered the day well, a pelting, drenching day when the water streamed

249
00:15:33,540 --> 00:15:37,137
down the window pane and the light indoors was too dull to read by.

250
00:15:37,137 --> 00:15:41,878
The boredom of the two children in the dark, cramped bedroom became unbearable.

251
00:15:41,878 --> 00:15:46,317
Winston whined and grizzled, made futile demands for food, fretted about the room

252
00:15:46,317 --> 00:15:49,200
pulling everything out of place and kicking the wainscoting until the

253
00:15:49,200 --> 00:15:53,580
neighbors banged on the wall, while the younger child wailed intermittently.

254
00:15:53,580 --> 00:15:58,378
In the end his mother said, 'Now be good, and I'll buy you a toy. A lovely toy—

255
00:15:58,378 --> 00:16:02,520
—you'll love it'; and then she had gone out in the rain, to a little general shop

256
00:16:02,520 --> 00:16:06,477
which was still sporadically open nearby, and came back with a cardboard box

257
00:16:06,477 --> 00:16:09,240
containing an outfit of Snakes and Ladders.

258
00:16:09,240 --> 00:16:12,297
He could still remember the smell of the damp cardboard.

259
00:16:12,297 --> 00:16:14,218
It was a miserable outfit.

260
00:16:14,218 --> 00:16:17,817
The board was cracked and the tiny wooden dice were so well-cut that they

261
00:16:17,817 --> 00:16:20,040
would hardly lie on their sides.

262
00:16:20,040 --> 00:16:24,419
Winston looked at the thing silkily and without interest. But then his mother lit

263
00:16:24,419 --> 00:16:27,119
a piece of candle and they sat down on the floor to play.

264
00:16:27,119 --> 00:16:31,080
Soon he was wildly excited and shouting with laughter as the tiddlywinks climbed

265
00:16:31,080 --> 00:16:34,977
hopefully up the ladders and then came slithering down the snakes again, almost

266
00:16:34,977 --> 00:16:39,718
to the starting point They played eight games, winning four each.

267
00:16:39,718 --> 00:16:43,860
His tiny sister, too young to understand what the game was about, had set propped

268
00:16:43,860 --> 00:16:47,340
up against a bolster, laughing because the others were laughing.

269
00:16:47,340 --> 00:16:52,977
For a whole afternoon they had all been happy together, as in his earlier childhood.

270
00:16:52,977 --> 00:16:57,779
He pushed the picture out of his mind. It was a false memory. He was troubled by

271
00:16:57,779 --> 00:16:59,580
false memories occasionally.

272
00:16:59,580 --> 00:17:03,000
They did not matter so long as one knew them for what they were.

273
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:05,759
Some things had happened, others had not happened.

274
00:17:05,759 --> 00:17:09,599
He turned back to the chessboard and picked up the white knight again.

275
00:17:09,599 --> 00:17:13,919
Almost in the same instant it dropped on the board with a clatter. He had started

276
00:17:13,919 --> 00:17:16,080
as though a pin had run into him.

277
00:17:16,080 --> 00:17:21,360
A shrilled trumpet call had pierced the air. It was the bulletin! Victory! It

278
00:17:21,360 --> 00:17:24,779
always meant victory when a trumpet call preceded the news.

279
00:17:24,779 --> 00:17:28,740
A sort of electric drill ran through the cafe Even the waiters had started and

280
00:17:28,740 --> 00:17:31,080
picked up their ears.

281
00:17:31,080 --> 00:17:34,439
The trumpets call had let loose an enormous volume of noise.

282
00:17:34,439 --> 00:17:38,457
.Already an excited voice was gabbling from the telescreen, but even as it

283
00:17:38,457 --> 00:17:42,419
started it was almost drowned by a roar of cheering from outside.

284
00:17:42,419 --> 00:17:45,119
The news had run around the streets like magic.

285
00:17:45,119 --> 00:17:48,659
He could hear just enough of what was issuing from the telescreen to realize

286
00:17:48,659 --> 00:17:53,099
that it had all happened as he had foreseen: a vast Seaborn armada had

287
00:17:53,099 --> 00:17:57,180
secretly assembled, a sudden blow in the enemy's rear, the white arrow tearing

288
00:17:57,180 --> 00:17:59,159
across the tail of the black.

289
00:17:59,159 --> 00:18:02,817
Fragments of triumphant phrases pushed themselves through the din

290
00:18:02,817 --> 00:18:07,977
fast strategic maneuver perfect coordination at a route half a million

291
00:18:07,977 --> 00:18:12,957
prisoners— —complete demoralization control of the whole of Africa— —bring the

292
00:18:12,957 --> 00:18:17,279
war within measurable distance of its end— —victory— —greatest victory in human

293
00:18:17,279 --> 00:18:21,540
history— —victory, victory, victory!'

294
00:18:21,540 --> 00:18:25,977
Under the table Winston's feet made convulsive movements. He had not stirred

295
00:18:25,977 --> 00:18:29,637
from his seat, but in his mind he was running, swiftly running, he was with the

296
00:18:29,637 --> 00:18:32,218
crowds outside, cheering himself deaf.

297
00:18:32,218 --> 00:18:35,040
He looked up again at the portrait of Big Brother.

298
00:18:35,040 --> 00:18:37,680
The colossus that bestowed the world!

299
00:18:37,680 --> 00:18:41,759
The rock against which the hordes of Asia dashed themselves in vain!

300
00:18:41,759 --> 00:18:45,477
He thought how 10 minutes ago— —yes, only 10 minutes— —there had still been

301
00:18:45,477 --> 00:18:48,718
equivocation in his heart as he wondered whether the news from the front would be

302
00:18:48,718 --> 00:18:53,040
a victory or defeat oh it was more than a Eurasian army that

303
00:18:53,040 --> 00:18:57,360
had perished! Much had changed in him since that first day in the Ministry of

304
00:18:57,360 --> 00:19:03,779
Love, but the final, indispensable, healing change had never happened, until this moment.

305
00:19:03,779 --> 00:19:07,317
The voice from the telescreen was still pouring forth its tale of prisoners and

306
00:19:07,317 --> 00:19:11,340
booty and slaughter, but the shouting outside had died down a little.

307
00:19:11,340 --> 00:19:15,898
The waiters were turning back to their work. One of them approached with the gin bottle.

308
00:19:15,898 --> 00:19:20,340
Winston, sitting in a blissful dream, paid no attention as his glass was filled up.

309
00:19:20,340 --> 00:19:23,817
He was not running or cheering any longer. He was back in the Ministry of

310
00:19:23,817 --> 00:19:26,939
Love, with everything forgiven, his soul whiter snow.

311
00:19:26,939 --> 00:19:31,080
He was in the public dock, confessing everything, implicating everybody.

312
00:19:31,080 --> 00:19:34,558
He was walking down the white-tailed corridor, with the feeling of walking in

313
00:19:34,558 --> 00:19:37,259
sunlight, and an armed guard at his back.

314
00:19:37,259 --> 00:19:40,919
The long hoped for bullet was entering his brain.

315
00:19:40,919 --> 00:19:45,840
He gazed up at the enormous fate 40 years it had taken him to learn what

316
00:19:45,840 --> 00:19:51,898
kind of smile was hidden beneath the dark mustache oh cruel, needless misunderstanding! O

317
00:19:51,898 --> 00:19:54,957
stubborn, self-willed exile from the loving breast!

318
00:19:54,957 --> 00:19:58,680
Two gin centered tears trickled down the sides of his nose.

319
00:19:58,680 --> 00:20:02,759
But it was all right, everything was all right, the struggle was finished. He had

320
00:20:02,759 --> 00:20:04,619
won the victory over himself.

321
00:20:04,619 --> 00:20:07,558
He loved Big Brother.

322
00:20:07,558 --> 00:20:09,000
THE END
